# C++ & UI editing rules

## Language & style

- **C++20** (`target_compile_features(... cxx_std_20)`). Match surrounding naming and include order.
- JUCE headers first, then project headers. Use `juce::` prefix consistently with existing files.
- Prefer extending existing types over new parallel abstractions.

## Audio & realtime safety

- Never allocate, lock, or call blocking I/O on the audio thread.
- UI updates from background threads must use `juce::MessageManager::callAsync` or existing weak-reference patterns (see `PluginScanThread` in `AudioEngine.cpp`).
- Engine mutations go through `AudioEngineManager`; check freeze/bypass guards before moving plugins.

## UI

- Observe `ProjectData` / `ValueTree` listeners; avoid duplicating state in component members.
- Use `Theme::` colours, fonts, and `uiSize()` scaling — not raw `juce::Colours::` or hard-coded 14px unless matching an existing local pattern.
- Tooltips: use `AerionTooltipWindow` where the rest of the file does.
- Large UI lives in `UIComponents.h` — keep new components consistent with existing section headers and paint methods.

## Plugins & formats

- VST3 hosting is enabled (`JUCE_PLUGINHOST_VST3=1`). AU is macOS-only.
- Plugin scan paths: Windows uses custom sanitised paths; **Linux uses JUCE defaults** (`~/.vst3`, `/usr/lib/vst3`, etc.). Do not paste Windows path logic into Linux builds.
- Preferred Linux audio device order in code: **JACK, then ALSA** (`AudioEngine.cpp`).

## Files to touch carefully

| Area | Files |
|------|-------|
| Main window / menus | `MainComponent.cpp` |
| Keymap | `Keymap.h` + consumers |
| Export | `Source/Export/*` |
| CMake / resources | `CMakeLists.txt`, `Resources/` |

## Tests

When changing `ProjectData` or `Keymap` serialisation, update or extend `AerionTests` (`Source/Tests/TestsMain.cpp`) and verify with:

```bash
cmake --build build --target AerionTests
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```
